# Sui Move Intro Course Project Structure

This is a Japanese translation of the official Sui Move intro course from [sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course](https://github.com/sui-foundation/sui-move-intro-course). It's organized as a progressive educational resource for Japanese learners to understand Sui Move development with hands-on examples.

## Course Organization

### Core Units

- **unit-one/**: Environment setup, project structure, basic types and functions
  - [hello_world](mdc:unit-one/example_projects/hello_world/) - Basic Move contract example
- **unit-two/**: Sui objects, ownership, capabilities, and events
  - [transcript](mdc:unit-two/example_projects/transcript/) - Object management examples
- **unit-three/**: Sui framework, generics, witnesses, tokens, and testing
  - [fungible_tokens](mdc:unit-three/example_projects/fungible_tokens/) - Token implementation
  - [locked_coin](mdc:unit-three/example_projects/locked_coin/) - Time-locked assets
  - [witness](mdc:unit-three/example_projects/witness/) - Witness pattern examples
- **unit-four/**: Collections, dynamic fields, marketplace contracts
  - [collections](mdc:unit-four/example_projects/collections/) - Data structures
  - [marketplace](mdc:unit-four/example_projects/marketplace/) - Trading platform
- **unit-five/**: Advanced patterns, PTBs, hot potato, kiosk system
  - [flashloan](mdc:unit-five/example_projects/flashloan/) - DeFi patterns
  - [kiosk](mdc:unit-five/example_projects/kiosk/) - NFT marketplace system

### Advanced Topics

- **advanced-topics/**: Specialized concepts like BCS encoding

### Learning Resources

- **exercises/**: Practice problems with answer keys
- **lessons/**: Detailed explanations in Japanese markdown
- **images/**: Visual aids and screenshots

## Key Files

- [Move.toml](mdc:Move.toml): Package configuration for each project
- [SUMMARY.md](mdc:SUMMARY.md): Course table of contents
- [book.toml](mdc:book.toml): mdBook configuration for course material

## Development Patterns

Each unit follows a consistent structure:

1. Conceptual lessons (\*.md files)
2. Example projects with working code
3. Exercises for practice
4. Progressive complexity from basic to advanced topics
